#: ../../library/turtle.rst:431 ../../library/turtle.rst:482
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:757 ../../library/turtle.rst:1301
msgid "a number"
msgstr "um número"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:218
msgid ""
"Move the turtle forward by the specified *distance*, in the direction the "
"turtle is headed."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para frente pela *distance* especificada, na direção em que "
"a tartaruga está indo."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:221
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(25)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(25.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(-75)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-50.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(25)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(25.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(-75)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-50.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:240
msgid ""
"Move the turtle backward by *distance*, opposite to the direction the turtle "
"is headed. The turtle's heading does not change."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para trás por *distance*, na direção oposta à direção em "
"que a tartaruga está indo. A direção da tartaruga não muda."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:249
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.backward(30)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-30.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.backward(30)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-30.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:264
msgid ""
"Turn the turtle right by the specified *angle*. The angle is measured in "
"degrees by default; the unit can be changed with :func:`degrees` or :func:"
"`radians`. How the heading is measured depends on the turtle mode, see :func:"
"`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Gira a tartaruga para direita pelo ângulo *angle* especificado. Por padrão, "
"o ângulo é medido em graus; a unidade pode ser alterada com :func:`degrees` "
"ou :func:`radians`. A forma como a direção é medida depende do modo da "
"tartaruga; consulte :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:275
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.right(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"337.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.right(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"337.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:290
msgid ""
"Turn the turtle left by the specified *angle*. The angle is measured in "
"degrees by default; the unit can be changed with :func:`degrees` or :func:"
"`radians`. How the heading is measured depends on the turtle mode, see :func:"
"`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Gira a tartaruga para esquerda pelo ângulo *angle* especificado. Por padrão, "
"o ângulo é medido em graus; a unidade pode ser alterada com :func:`degrees` "
"ou :func:`radians`. A forma como a direção é medida depende do modo da "
"tartaruga; consulte :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:301
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.left(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.left(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:315
msgid "a number or a pair/vector of numbers"
msgstr "um número ou um par/vetor de números"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:316 ../../library/turtle.rst:348
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:349 ../../library/turtle.rst:483
msgid "a number or ``None``"
msgstr "um número ou ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:318
msgid ""
"Move the turtle to an absolute position. If *y* is ``None``, *x* must be a "
"pair of coordinates or a :class:`Vec2D`, for example as returned by :func:"
"`pos`. If the pen is down, a line is drawn. The turtle's heading does not "
"change."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para uma posição absoluta. Se *y* for ``None``, *x* deve "
"ser um par de coordenadas ou um :class:`Vec2D`, como, por exemplo, o valor "
"retornado por :func:`pos`. Se a caneta estiver abaixada, uma linha é "
"desenhada. A orientação da tartaruga não muda."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:329
msgid ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(60,30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,30.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto((20,80))\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,80.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(tp)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(60,30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,30.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto((20,80))\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,80.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(tp)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:350
msgid "a boolean"
msgstr "um valor booleano"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:352
msgid ""
"Move turtle to an absolute position. Unlike goto(x, y), a line will not be "
"drawn. The turtle's orientation does not change. If currently filling, the "
"polygon(s) teleported from will be filled after leaving, and filling will "
"begin again after teleporting. This can be disabled with fill_gap=True, "
"which makes the imaginary line traveled during teleporting act as a fill "
"barrier like in goto(x, y)."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para uma posição absoluta. Ao contrário de goto(x, y), uma "
"linha não será desenhada. A orientação da tartaruga não muda. Se estiver "
"sendo preenchido no momento, o(s) polígono(s) teletransportado(s) será(ão) "
"preenchido(s) após sair, e o preenchimento começará novamente após o "
"teletransporte. Isso pode ser desabilitado com fill_gap=True, o que faz com "
"que a linha imaginária percorrida durante o teletransporte atue como uma "
"barreira de preenchimento como em goto(x, y)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:365
msgid ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(60)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(y=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(20, 30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,30.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(60)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(y=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(20, 30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,30.00)"

